Complete the binary128 datatype separation from upstream PR #13714.

Keep Fortran COMPLEX*32 enabled with its matching ISO_C_BINDING kind and
quad-complex SUM/PROD kernels. Append the operation slot so existing indices
remain unchanged. Preserve x87 long-double external32 conversion, while
binary128 complex needs only byte-order conversion, not x87 conversion.
Correct the upstream backport's inverted _Quad availability guard as well.

The installed regression tests cover both Fortran quad types and the distinct
C long-double types, including independently specified external32 bytes.

